  "definition": "CWB stands for counterproductive work behavior: actions by employees that harm an organization or the people in it. It can include behaviors such as abuse, sabotage, withdrawal, theft, and in digital work settings, things like hiding information, manipulating or destroying data, or misusing technology resources.",
